{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_turbulence_spectrum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_turbulence_spectrum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_turbulence_spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_turbulence_spectrum","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L208-L236","doc":"**q-deformed energy cascade and modified Kolmogorov spectrum**\n([`prop:q-turbulence-spectrum`]) — the resolving declaration for\n`lean.ref` `qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_turbulence_spectrum`.\n\n**Conditional on the cascade model** (`QTurbulenceCascadeModel`,\nexplicit instance binder per §3b-cond): conjoins the four\nsub-claims, now **sorry-free**. (i) and (ii) hold definitionally\n(`E_q` / `transferRate` are honest `def`s of the manuscript\nformulas); (iii) the cascade-depth bound is **derived** from the\ndissipation-cutoff hypothesis `q^N ≤ Re_q^{3/4}`\n(`QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_of_cutoff`); (iv) the\nspectral-gap positivity is **derived** from `q > 1`\n(`QTurbulence.ΔE_gap_pos`) via monotonicity of the symmetric\nq-integer and of `x ↦ x^{−5/3}`.  No conjunct projects a class\nfield; the only assumed content is the named cutoff hypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-turbulence-spectrum","label":"prop:q-turbulence-spectrum","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-turbulence-spectrum.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_unconstrained_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_unconstrained_false","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L190-L204","doc":"**The unconditional form of claim (iii) is refutable as written** — the\nbase class never relates the fields the conclusion names, so\n`∀ instances` admits ones that simply disagree. Not an open gap: no\nunconditional `sorry` could ever be discharged. The fix is\n`QTurbulenceCascadeModel` above (bean `qou-octr`, criterion §10\n`proof-unclosable-context-sorry`): the cutoff hypothesis is exactly\nwhat this counterexample violates (`2^1000000 > 2^{3/4}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_of_cutoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_of_cutoff","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L172-L188","doc":"Claim (iii), **derived** from the cascade-model cutoff (conditional\non `QTurbulenceCascadeModel`, Mathlib `_of_` naming): taking `log`\nof `q^N ≤ Re_q^{3/4}` gives `N·log q ≤ ¾·log Re_q`, and dividing by\n`log q > 0` (from `q > 1`) yields the depth bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.cutoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.cutoff","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L168-L168","doc":"Dissipation cutoff: all active modes fit under the Kolmogorov\nscale, `q ^ N_modes ≤ Re_q ^ (3/4 : ℝ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.toQTurbulenceSpectrumContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel.toQTurbulenceSpectrumContext","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L165-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceCascadeModel","kind":"class","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L151-L168","doc":"**Cascade model** for claim (iii) (the fix demanded by\n`finite_cascade_depth_unconstrained_false` below, bean `qou-octr`):\nthe single physical input of the Kolmogorov dissipation-cutoff\nargument, as an explicit hypothesis.  On the geometric mode ladder\nthe `N`-th active mode sits at wavenumber scale `q^N`, and the\nclassical cutoff argument places every active mode below the\ndissipation scale `Re^{3/4}` — the multiplicative bound\n`q^N_modes ≤ Re_q^{3/4}`.\n\nThe field is a *hypothesis in the shape of the physical model*, not\nthe conclusion: the depth bound `N ≤ ¾·log Re_q / log q` is derived\nfrom it by the log/division algebra in\n`QTurbulence.finite_cascade_depth_of_cutoff` (§3b-cond item 5:\nthe class carries the input, the theorem does the derivation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.ΔE_gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.ΔE_gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L130-L147","doc":"Claim (iv), **derived sorry-free**: the spectral gap is positive.\n\n`[1]_q = 1 < q + q⁻¹ = [2]_q` (from `q > 1`), the map `x ↦ x^{−5/3}`\nis strictly antitone on positives, and `C_q, ε^{2/3} > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_two","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L124-L128","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_one","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L118-L122","doc":"`[1]_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.q_sub_inv_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.q_sub_inv_pos","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L111-L116","doc":"`q − q⁻¹ > 0` for `q > 1` (the symmetric q-integer's denominator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.ΔE_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.ΔE_gap","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L105-L109","doc":"The spectral gap `ΔE_gap = C_q · ε^{2/3} · ([1]_q^{−5/3} − [2]_q^{−5/3})`\nbelow the fundamental mode. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.transferRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.transferRate","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L99-L103","doc":"Claim (ii) as a **definition**: the mode-to-mode transfer rate\n`T_{k→k+1} = ε · ([k+1]_q^{2/3} − [k]_q^{2/3}) / ([k+1]_q − [k]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.E_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.E_q","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L93-L97","doc":"Claim (i) as a **definition**: the q-deformed Kolmogorov spectrum\n`E_q(k) = C_q · ε^{2/3} · [k]_q^{−5/3} / ([k]_q / k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.**  The body is already the\ncanonical one — the equation holds by `rfl` — so what the local `def` adds is\nonly the binding of `q` to the context.  It is kept for that reason; the\nidentity records that no second convention is in play here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulence.qInt","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L81-L84","doc":"The symmetric q-integer `[k]_q = (q^k − q^{−k})/(q − q^{−1})`\n(the `.md`'s convention; `[k]_q → k` as `q → 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.C_q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.C_q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.C_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.C_q","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The q-dependent Kolmogorov constant `C_q` (positive physical\ninput). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.ε_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.ε_pos","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.ε","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.ε","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The energy dissipation rate `ε` (positive physical input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.N_modes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.N_modes","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Number of active modes in the cascade (opaque physical datum;\nclaim (iii) bounds it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.Re_q_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.Re_q_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.Re_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.Re_q","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Planck–Reynolds number `Re_q = 2 / (q − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.q","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QTurbulenceSpectrumContext","kind":"class","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_turbulence_spectrum.lean#L55-L75","doc":"Data for the `q_turbulence_spectrum` claim.  All fields are *inputs*\n(the substrate parameter, the Planck--Reynolds number, the physical\nconstants with their positivity, and the opaque active-mode count);\nnone is one of the four conclusions. ","signatureChunk":0}]}